     "description": "Chris Pronger joined the Anaheim Ducks ahead of the 2006\u201307 season, bringing size, snarl, and elite two-way play to a blue line already anchored by Scott Niedermayer. In his first year with the club, Pronger helped lead Anaheim to its first Stanley Cup title in franchise history. In a game versus the San Jose Sharks, he showcased his trademark cannon from the point, blasting home a one-timer in the Ducks 3\u20131 win. Pronger spent three seasons in Anaheim, solidifying the Ducks as a perennial contender during his time with the team.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
